  "summary": "A full-containment LNG tank stores liquefied natural gas at about −162 °C. An inner tank of 9 % nickel steel holds the liquid; thick insulation limits heat leak; an outer pre-stressed concrete wall and roof can contain the liquid and vapour if the inner tank leaks. Pumps in columns send LNG out from the top, and boil-off gas is removed and recovered.",
